 # Working notes: feaa89c467a0
+
+## Current repair — exact class-count control, 2026-10-24
+
+Assignment `review-7558014547ea824f` found a source-bound control defect in
+version 3.0.0: `difficulty="easy", n_classes=4, seed=0` requested four
+dihedral classes but produced only three. No connected three-cell polyomino has
+eight distinct D4 images, so `_asym_motif(3)` exhausted its search and silently
+returned a four-cell fallback that could collide with the genuine four-cell
+class.
+
+Version 3.0.1 removes the impossible three-cell claim, samples exact-size
+asymmetric motifs only for sizes 4–9, and provides a connected eight-image
+fallback for every supported size. The canonical Racket rule and rule hash
+`c2216441944e` are unchanged. The focused regression sweeps 192 combinations
+(three difficulty settings, one to four requested classes, and 16 seeds); all
+realize the exact requested class count and every panel has eight D4 images. A
+protected-Racket receipt covers 24 representative cases and matches an
+independent relation matrix 24/24. Evidence is retained at
+`checks/peer-feaa-tdd-green/result.json` and
+`checks/feaa89c467a0-class-control/verification.json`.
+
+This optional peer change is a repair proposal, not owner acceptance. Because
+the generator source hash changed, catalog approval/source binding must be
+refreshed by the owner. Historical lint findings unrelated to class-count
+realization were not expanded or claimed fixed.
+
 
 Record design decisions, hypotheses, review findings, and unresolved questions here.
 Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
